{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  The somm answers in bottle codes and the theme resolves them here. That means
  the catalogue has to cover every code the somm can return — the bottles AND
  the sets, since "SET" is a real answer. Two collections, because the store
  keeps them separate (the-range / non-sets).

  If this is empty the somm still answers, but the pick cards silently render
  nothing, which is exactly what happened when neither collection was set.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bottles = section.settings.pick_collection | default: collections[settings.core_range_collection] | default: collections['the-range']
  assign sets = section.settings.sets_collection | default: collections['non-sets']
-%}

<section class="non-hero" data-non-somm-root>
  <div class="non-hero__copy">
    {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
      <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <h1 class="non-hero__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>

    {%- if section.settings.blurb != blank -%}
      <p class="non-hero__blurb">{{ section.settings.blurb }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      THE WAY IN, ahead of the way to ask.

      The hero explained the proposition well and then offered exactly one
      interaction: the Somm. A customer who already knew they wanted a bottle
      had no obvious path to one, and a customer who did not want to talk to an
      assistant had none at all. The Somm is the interesting thing here; it
      should not be the only apparent thing.

      So: shopping first, asking second, and the second is a real button rather
      than a hint that the field below exists. It focuses the Somm rather than
      navigating, because the Somm is already on this page — sending someone
      elsewhere to reach something six inches down would be theatre.

      Rendered only when a link is set, so an unconfigured store shows what it
      showed before rather than a button going nowhere.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.cta_shop_url != blank -%}
      <div class="non-hero__ctas">
        <a class="non-btn non-hero__cta" href="{{ section.settings.cta_shop_url }}">
          {{ section.settings.cta_shop_label }}
        </a>
        {%- if settings.somm_enabled and section.settings.cta_ask_label != blank -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="non-btn non-btn--ghost non-hero__cta"
            data-non-somm-open
            data-somm-surface="homepage_hero"
            data-somm-context="home">
            {{ section.settings.cta_ask_label }}
          </button>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      NON Somm. The query goes to an external endpoint (a Cloudflare Worker);
      the seeds below are the canned answers from the design and are used both
      as one-tap prompts and as the offline fallback when no endpoint is set.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      THE MOBILE ENTRY — a way in, not the whole conversation.

      The inline form below is the right shape on a desktop, where it sits in a
      wide column with room for a field, a button, a live dot and five chips.
      On a 390px phone the same markup was 226px of the hero — the field, the
      chips and the orb pushed the picture off the first screen and the range
      1,226px down the page.

      So on a phone the Somm is announced and opened, and the conversation
      happens in the sheet where there is room for it. This is a BUTTON that
      looks like a field rather than a real input: a second focusable text field
      that only exists to open a dialog containing another text field is a trap
      for anyone using a keyboard or a screen reader, and iOS would raise the
      keyboard against a control that cannot receive typing.

      Exactly one of this and the form below is in the document at any width —
      the other is display:none, which takes it out of the accessibility tree
      as well as off the screen. Nothing is announced twice.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      THE PAIRING PAGE'S SOMM BLOCK, not a second design of one.

      This was rebuilt as a bespoke composition — .non-somm-entry, an orb in a
      grid column, a button dressed as a field. It indented the bar and the
      chips 120px past the hero's left edge while the eyebrow, headline, blurb
      and buttons all sat flush at 46, so the hero had a ragged edge with a
      faint glow in the gutter.

      The site already has this component and it is right on /pages/pairing and
      /pages/stockists: .non-somm wraps .non-somm__bar (caret, field, ASK) with
      .non-somm__seeds beneath, and the orb is .non-somm::before. Using those
      class names means it inherits every one of those rules — the orb's size,
      blur, opacity and position included — and the three surfaces cannot drift
      apart again, because there is one set of styles.

      THE ONE DIFFERENCE, and it is behaviour not appearance: this does not
      answer inline. It has no [data-non-somm] hook, so somm.js does not bind a
      controller to it. Focusing the field or submitting it opens the shared
      sheet and hands over whatever was typed — one Somm, one transcript, as
      the brief requires. The markup is the pairing page's; only the wiring
      differs.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.somm_enabled -%}
    <form class="non-somm" data-non-somm-inline data-non-somm-hero role="search"
      data-somm-surface="homepage_hero" data-somm-context="home">
      <div class="non-somm__bar">
        <span class="non-somm__caret" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="somm-hero-{{ section.id }}">
          {{ 'sections.somm.placeholder' | t }}
        </label>
        <div class="non-somm__field">
          <input
          id="somm-hero-{{ section.id }}"
          class="non-somm__input"
          type="search"
          name="query"
          autocomplete="off"
          {%- comment -%}
            BOTH NAMES, for the two controllers that read this field.

            somm-sheet.js takes the typed text from `[data-non-somm-hero-input]`
            when it forwards to the sheet on a phone. somm.js resolves its own
            field with `form.querySelector('[data-non-somm-input]')` — the
            generic hook every other Somm uses — so without it the inline bind
            above the breakpoint found no input, read no query and returned
            silently. Bound, submitted, nothing asked.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          data-non-somm-input
          data-non-somm-hero-input
            placeholder="{{ section.settings.placeholder | escape }}">

          {%- comment -%}
            THE SHIMMER CANNOT LIVE ON THE PLACEHOLDER.

          `::placeholder` takes colour, font and opacity and nothing else - no
          background, so no `background-clip: text`, so no gradient and no
          animation. The shimmering line everywhere else on this site is a
          gradient clipped to letterforms, and a real placeholder physically
          cannot carry it.

          So the shimmer is a real element sitting over the field, and the
          native placeholder stays exactly where it was underneath: it is what a
          screen reader and a no-CSS render get, and what shows if this element
          ever fails to paint. The ghost is aria-hidden so the two are never
          announced as one string, and pointer-events: none so it cannot take a
          click meant for the input.

          It hides itself through `:placeholder-shown` on the input beside it -
          CSS, not script, so it cannot fall out of step with what is typed.
        {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="non-somm__ghost" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.settings.placeholder }}</span>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="non-somm__submit">{{ 'sections.somm.ask' | t }}</button>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The same three chips, in the pairing page's own chip class so they
        match it exactly. They carry the full question rather than a short
        label, because at this width there is room for the sentence and the
        sentence is the better invitation.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign all_seeds = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'seed' -%}
      {%- assign flagged_count = 0 -%}
      {%- for block in all_seeds -%}
        {%- if block.settings.show_on_mobile -%}
          {%- assign flagged_count = flagged_count | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if all_seeds.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="non-somm__seeds">
          {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
          {%- for block in all_seeds -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              FOUR, not three. Three was the ceiling everywhere while the chip
              row wrapped onto a second line on a phone and cost the hero its
              height. That row scrolls horizontally now, so a fourth costs
              nothing above the fold and gives the Somm one more way in.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if shown >= 4 -%}{% break %}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if flagged_count > 0 and block.settings.show_on_mobile != true -%}
              {%- continue -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="non-somm__seed"
              {%- comment -%}
                BOTH HOOKS, and which one acts depends on the width.

                `data-non-somm-seed` is what somm.js's root listener reads, so
                on a desktop the chip asks inline like the field beside it.
                `data-non-somm-open` is the sheet's, so on a phone it still
                opens the sheet. somm-sheet.js ignores the second above the
                breakpoint precisely so they cannot both fire.

                The canned answer travels with it because that list is also the
                offline fallback: a chip that reaches somm.js with no vetted
                copy asks the Worker for a real answer instead, which is the
                right behaviour and not the fast one.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              data-non-somm-seed
              data-answer="{{ block.settings.answer | escape }}"
              data-picks="{{ block.settings.picks | escape }}"
              data-non-somm-open
              data-somm-surface="homepage_hero"
              data-somm-context="home"
              data-somm-intent="{{ block.settings.intent | escape }}"
              data-somm-prompt="{{ block.settings.label | escape }}"
              {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {{ block.settings.short_label | default: block.settings.label }}
            </button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        THE ANSWER, IN THE PAGE.

        The Somm used to open a panel over the homepage to say what it thought,
        which reads as a popup arriving on top of the site rather than as the
        hero answering the question it just asked for. This is where the answer
        goes on a desktop: under the bar, in the same column, in the composition.

        Hidden until there is something to say — somm.js clears `hidden` on
        [data-non-somm-answer] and on the stream inside it. Below the
        breakpoint it stays hidden and the sheet does the talking, because a
        transcript unrolling inside a 402px hero would push the range off the
        page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="non-somm__answer" data-non-somm-answer hidden>
        <p class="non-somm__stream" data-non-somm-stream></p>
        <div class="non-somm__picks" data-non-somm-picks hidden></div>
      </div>
    </form>

    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      THE HERO NO LONGER CONTAINS A SOMM.

      It used to hold the whole thing: a field, a submit, a live dot, five
      chips and the answer panel — while the phone opened a sheet instead. Two
      implementations of one feature, one per breakpoint, with two transcripts
      that knew nothing about each other. Ask on a desktop, resize, and the
      conversation was gone.

      There is one Somm now and it is the sheet, at every width. The hero keeps
      what a hero should: the proposition, the supporting line, Shop the range,
      Ask the Somm, and three short prompts. Everything below opens the same
      component and continues the same transcript.

      THE SEEDS SURVIVE AS DATA. They were the offline fallback and the chip
      source, and both still need them — but as a JSON payload rather than as a
      form full of buttons nobody can see. A hidden control is still a control;
      a script tag is not.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script type="application/json" data-non-somm-seeds>
      [
        {%- assign seed_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'seed' -%}
        {%- for block in seed_blocks -%}
          {
            "label": {{ block.settings.label | json }},
            "short": {{ block.settings.short_label | default: block.settings.label | json }},
            "answer": {{ block.settings.answer | json }},
            "picks": {{ block.settings.picks | default: '' | split: ',' | json }},
            "intent": {{ block.settings.intent | default: '' | json }},
            "mobile": {{ block.settings.show_on_mobile | default: false | json }}
          }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ]
    </script>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Hero media. Slide blocks make it a carousel, matching the current site; a
    single slide just renders as a still. The imagery already lives on NON's
    own Shopify CDN, so a slide can carry either an upload or a URL, and the
    upload wins.

    The first slide is eager and high priority — it is the LCP element. Every
    other slide is lazy, so a five-slide hero costs one image on first paint.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- assign slides = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'slide' -%}

  {%- if slides.size > 0 -%}
    <div
      class="non-hero__media non-carousel"
      data-non-carousel
      data-interval="{{ section.settings.slide_interval | times: 1000 }}"
      {% if slides.size > 1 %}aria-roledescription="carousel"{% endif %}
      aria-label="NON">
      {%- for block in slides -%}
        <div
          class="non-carousel__slide{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"
          data-non-slide
          {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          {%- liquid
            assign loading = 'lazy'
            assign defer_slide = true
            if forloop.first
              assign loading = 'eager'
              assign defer_slide = false
            endif
          -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            defer_slide is computed HERE, not written as `defer: forloop.first
            == false` in the render tag. Liquid does not evaluate a comparison
            in an argument position: it passed `forloop.first` straight through
            and dropped the `== false`, so the FIRST slide was deferred and the
            other four loaded eagerly — precisely backwards, and it looked
            plausible in the diff.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
            {{
              block.settings.image
              | image_url: width: 1400, format: 'webp'
              | image_tag:
                loading: loading,
                widths: '480,760,1000,1400',
                alt: block.settings.alt | default: shop.name
            }}
          {%- elsif block.settings.image_url != blank -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              First slide eager, the rest deferred. They are stacked, so they
              are all in the viewport and lazy loading does nothing for them.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {% render 'cdn-image',
               url: block.settings.image_url,
               alt: block.settings.alt,
               sizes: '(min-width: 1440px) 38vw, (min-width: 860px) 420px, 100vw',
               eager: forloop.first,
               defer: defer_slide %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- if slides.size > 1 -%}
        <div class="non-carousel__dots" data-non-carousel-dots role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a slide">
          {%- for block in slides -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="non-carousel__dot{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"
              data-non-carousel-dot
              role="tab"
              aria-selected="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
              aria-label="Slide {{ forloop.index }} of {{ slides.size }}"></button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.caption != blank -%}
        <div class="non-hero__caption">{{ section.settings.caption }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

  {%- elsif section.settings.image != blank or section.settings.image_url != blank -%}
    <div class="non-hero__media">
      {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
        {{
          section.settings.image
          | image_url: width: 1000, format: 'webp'
          | image_tag: loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', widths: '420,640,840,1000', alt: section.settings.image.alt | default: shop.name
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        {% render 'cdn-image',
           url: section.settings.image_url,
           sizes: '(min-width: 1440px) 38vw, (min-width: 860px) 420px, 100vw',
           eager: true %}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.caption != blank -%}
        <div class="non-hero__caption">{{ section.settings.caption }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  Catalogue for the somm's pick cards. The API answers with codes ("NON3");
  this maps a code to the real Shopify product so the card links, images and
  prices stay live.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/json" data-non-catalogue>
  {
    {%- assign seen = '' -%}
    {%- for product in bottles.products -%}
      {%- capture code %}{% render 'non-code', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
      {%- assign code = code | strip -%}
      {%- assign marker = '|' | append: code | append: '|' -%}
      {%- unless seen contains marker -%}
        {%- assign seen = seen | append: marker -%}
        {%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless -%}
        {{ code | json }}: {
          "title": {{ product.title | json }},
          "url": {{ product.url | json }},
          "image": {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 200, format: 'webp' | json }},
          "price": {{ product.price | money | json }},
          "note": {{ product.metafields.custom.profile | metafield_text | default: product.metafields.custom.tastes | metafield_text | default: '' | truncate: 44 | json }},
          "variantId": {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | json }},
          "available": {{ product.available | json }}
        }
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- comment -%} "SET" comes from whichever set is listed first. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for product in sets.products limit: 6 -%}
      {%- capture code %}{% render 'non-code', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
      {%- assign code = code | strip -%}
      {%- assign marker = '|' | append: code | append: '|' -%}
      {%- unless seen contains marker -%}
        {%- assign seen = seen | append: marker -%}
        ,{{ code | json }}: {
          "title": {{ product.title | json }},
          "url": {{ product.url | json }},
          "image": {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 200, format: 'webp' | json }},
          "price": {{ product.price | money | json }},
          "note": {{ product.metafields.custom.profile | metafield_text | default: '' | truncate: 44 | json }},
          "variantId": {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | json }},
          "available": {{ product.available | json }}
        }
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  }
</script>

<script src="{{ 'somm.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'carousel.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Hero + NON Somm",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "0.0% alcohol · not a mocktail"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Cooked, not de-alcoholised."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "blurb",
      "label": "Blurb",
      "default": "Fruit, tannin, salt and acid, built from zero at 0.0%. Tell the somm what's on the table and it will tell you what to pour."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "placeholder",
      "label": "Input placeholder",
      "info": "Shown shimmering in the bar until someone types. Keep it short - it has to fit on one line beside the Ask button.",
      "default": "Ask the NON Somm anything"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "mobile_placeholder",
      "label": "Phone prompt",
      "info": "The line inside the Somm button on a phone. Shorter than the desktop placeholder — it sits in a 320px field. Falls back to the placeholder above.",
      "default": "What's on the table?"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "somm_bg",
      "label": "Somm box background",
      "info": "The panel behind the somm. Leave empty for the theme default."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "somm_border",
      "label": "Somm box border"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_live",
      "label": "Show the live dot",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "live_label",
      "label": "Live label",
      "default": "Somm live"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "somm_dot_colour",
      "label": "Live dot colour",
      "info": "The one deliberate colour on an otherwise monochrome site. Set it to white to remove the exception."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Hero image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "image_url",
      "label": "Hero image URL",
      "info": "Used only when no image is uploaded. Defaults to the design's hero on NON's CDN.",
      "default": "https://www.non.world/cdn/shop/t/91/assets/non-home-hero-main-1.webp?v=85646433329311323311783460768"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "caption",
      "label": "Image caption",
      "default": "Built like a dish. Bottled at 0.0%."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "slide_interval",
      "label": "Seconds per slide",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "s",
      "default": 6,
      "info": "Only applies with more than one slide. Auto-advance is skipped entirely for anyone who prefers reduced motion."
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "pick_collection",
      "label": "Bottles the somm can recommend",
      "info": "Defaults to Theme settings, then to the-range."
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "sets_collection",
      "label": "Sets the somm can recommend",
      "info": "Needed for the code SET to resolve. Defaults to non-sets."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font_family",
      "label": "Font",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "Theme default"
        },
        {
          "value": "sans",
          "label": "Helvetica (all text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "mono",
          "label": "JetBrains Mono (all text)"
        }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "text_scale",
      "label": "Text size",
      "min": 70,
      "max": 150,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Scales every text size in this section together."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "section_padding",
      "label": "Vertical padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Hero buttons"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_shop_url",
      "label": "Shop link",
      "info": "The primary action. Leave empty to hide both buttons."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_shop_label",
      "label": "Shop button",
      "default": "Shop the range"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_ask_label",
      "label": "Ask button",
      "default": "Ask the Somm",
      "info": "Moves focus to the Somm field below rather than opening a page. Leave empty to hide it."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "slide",
      "name": "Hero slide",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Image"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "image_url",
          "label": "Image URL",
          "info": "Used only when no image is uploaded."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "alt",
          "label": "Alt text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "seed",
      "name": "Suggested question",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Question"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "answer",
          "label": "Canned answer",
          "info": "Also the offline fallback when the API is unreachable."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "picks",
          "label": "Bottle codes",
          "info": "Comma separated, e.g. NON3,NON1"
        },
